  "transcriptContext": "Knox’s original example on our table: you hold A♠ J♠ and the board runs K♦ Q♠ 4♣ 8♥ 2♦, heads-up against Ace Andy with 300 in the pot and 850 behind each. The pot, the stacks and the line that built them (you raised before the flop and bet the flop and the turn, and Ace Andy called both) are given for the exercise; Knox does not speak them. The hand is dealt as he says your line, the board runs out as he sets up the two questions, your two cards light as he names ace-jack, the king and queen lift as he names the strong hands your line represents, your ace rings as he says it blocks some of the strongest calls, and Ace Andy checks as he says villain checks. Beside the table, the two questions, the hands your line represents and his capped range with many one-pair hands appear only as he says them, and that range is marked as a given read, not his cards. Poor showdown value is his description, not an equity figure. The film recommends no action, shows no bet and turns over no opponent card. The original voice and speaking animation play continuously at their original speed.",
